.TH EGGHEAD 7 "April 2026" "egghead 0.1.0" "Egghead Manual"
.SH NAME
egghead \- concepts and architecture
.SH DESCRIPTION
Egghead is a personal knowledge base with AI agents that live inside it.
.PP
Under the hood: a record-store-first, graph-topology multi-agent system
with sparse activation and graduated mutation control, built on
actor-model supervision primitives.
.SH RECORDS
Records are markdown files with optional YAML frontmatter. Each
record has an id derived from its filename (e.g.
.I design/overview.md
becomes
.IR design/overview ).
.PP
Records can have tags, explicit links to other records, and
wikilinks in the body text (e.g.
.BR [[other-record]] ).
An SQLite index provides full-text search, link traversal, and
backlink discovery. The index is derived and rebuildable from
the source files.
.PP
Record classes:
.TP
.B durable
Long-lived knowledge (default).
.TP
.B inbox
Incoming, unprocessed.
.TP
.B deliberation
Agent conversation transcripts.
.TP
.B agent
Agent definition (body is system prompt).
.SH AGENTS
Agents are records with
.BR "class: agent" .
The record body serves as the agent's system prompt (disposition).
Frontmatter configures model, capabilities, and tags.
.PP
Example agent frontmatter:
.nf

---
class: agent
model: anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6
capabilities: [search, record_read, record_append]
tags: [research, patterns]
---

.fi
.PP
Available capabilities:
.TP
.B search
Full-text search of the record store.
.TP
.B record_read
Read full record contents.
.TP
.B record_append
Create new records.
.TP
.B record_modify
Modify existing records.
.PP
A built-in agent called
.B Index
is always available. It helps navigate the record store and
uses the model configured as
.B default_model
in the config file.
.SH CHAT ROOMS
Agents collaborate in chat rooms with a shared transcript.
Agents self-select via @-mentions and relevance gating.
The coordinator manages activation order using TF-IDF
scoring against agent dispositions.
.PP
Agents that have nothing to add respond with [PASS]. Staggered
activation ensures each agent sees prior responses before
composing its own.
.SH MCP
Egghead exposes 15 tools via the Model Context Protocol (MCP).
Two transports are available:
.TP
.B Stdio
JSON-RPC over stdin/stdout. Start with
.BR "egghead mcp" .
Configure in
.I .mcp.json
for editor integration.
.TP
.B HTTP
POST to
.I /mcp
on the web server. Available when running
.BR "egghead serve" .
.SH DESIGN PRINCIPLES
.TP
.B Knowledge graph as institution
Records survive agents. Agents are staff, not the organization.
.TP
.B Plain files are the universal interface
Markdown on a filesystem, not a database.
.TP
.B Graph topology, sparse activation
Agents collaborate through shared transcripts with self-selection.
.TP
.B Capability-based mutation control
Reads are free; writes follow a graduated spectrum.
